we've been running some surveys outside  of our testing sites so after you've  registered and you've  then turned up at the testing site and  we've asked people  whether or not they do actually have  symptoms and we surveyed so if i give  you the details 24  000 people at 25 regional and local  testing sites between the 1st and the  4th of september  the secretary of state referred to this  earlier today and this data will be  published online  27 of people said they were there  because they'd been in contact with  someone  who had tested positive but they didn't  have symptoms themselves  now this isn't the first time the blame  has been shifted on  to the modeling but ultimately the  responsibility must lie with the  government  the warning signs were there
 

